 objects are able to render tables as an array of strings where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each string is representing a line of text. A generator can be used by several threads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at the same time, which is why renderers are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": they have to be immutable or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"synchronize their state.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TableRenderer"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/StringGenerator/TableRenderer","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TableRenderer"}],"role":"symbol","title":"StringGenerator.TableRenderer","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/stringgenerator/tablerenderer"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/SyntaxHighlighting":{"abstract":[{"text":"Color the code of fenced code blocks in attributed strings and terminal output, or highlight code on its own.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/SyntaxHighlighting","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Highlighting Code","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/syntaxhighlighting"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TableDescriptor":{"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"TableDescriptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value encapsulates all information needed to render","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a table, including metadata about each column (to determine how columns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are organized).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TableDescriptor"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TableDescriptor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kin